# VelChat dev flavor — PUBLIC build config only (never secrets).
# Development = `dev` branch → Render, topology `axis6` (six services behind one edge gateway).
# Clients only ever talk to the EDGE GATEWAY; it routes to whichever service owns the path.
# Source of truth: D:\Velchat\docs\RUNBOOK.md §0b "Base URLs".
# NOTE: Render free services sleep after ~15 min idle — the first request wakes them (slow).
# For a LOCAL backend instead, use http://localhost:8080 + `pnpm reverse` (adb reverse 8080).
ENV=dev
API_BASE_URL=https://velchat-edge-gateway-2aje.onrender.com
# WS bypasses the edge gateway on Render ON PURPOSE: `apps/edge-gateway` has no `/ws` route and
# no `server.on('upgrade')` handler, so an upgrade sent there can never complete. Only production
# (Azure) proxies /ws, via Caddy. Do NOT "fix" this to the gateway host — it will not connect.
WS_URL=wss://velchat-realtime-service-2aje.onrender.com/ws
